<div class="sp-wrap">
  <div class="sp-title">STACK Infrastructure &mdash; SPCC Spill Prevention, Control &amp; Countermeasure</div>
  <div class="sp-subtitle">7300 Souder Road, New Albany, Ohio &nbsp;|&nbsp; SPCC Plan Version 3.0 &nbsp;|&nbsp; SPCC Coordinator: Matt Honaker, COM &nbsp;|&nbsp; 40 CFR &sect;112</div>
  <table class="sp-table">
    <thead><tr><th class="sp-corner"></th><th class="sp-ph" style="background:#2c5f8a">1 &mdash; Prevention &amp;<br>Routine Operations</th><th class="sp-ph" style="background:#5a3080">2 &mdash; Inspection &amp;<br>Monitoring</th><th class="sp-ph" style="background:#8B2500">3 &mdash; Spill Discovery &amp;<br>Immediate Response</th><th class="sp-ph" style="background:#8a5a00">4 &mdash; Cleanup &amp;<br>Regulatory Reporting</th><th class="sp-ph" style="background:#1a5c6b">5 &mdash; Documentation &amp;<br>Plan Maintenance</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody><tr><td class="sp-lbl" style="background:#1e3a5f">All<br>Personnel</td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#eef3f9"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#dce9f5;border-color:#2c5f8a;color:#111111"><ul><li>Follow all STACK safety &amp; SPCC procedures</li><li><b>Oil Transfers:</b> monitor continuously; verify available capacity before filling</li><li>No smoking / open flames within 25 ft of oil storage or transfer area</li><li>Close and secure all valves &amp; manholes after transfers</li><li>Chock vehicle wheels; do not depart until transfer lines are fully disconnected</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#eef3f9"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#ece4f5;border-color:#5a3080;color:#111111"><ul><li>Report any observed leaks, corrosion, odors, or staining to SPCC Coordinator</li><li>Conduct periodic walkthroughs; report emergency conditions per company policy</li><li>Do not attempt repairs without proper authorization</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#eef3f9"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fce8e4;border-color:#8B2500;color:#111111"><ul><li><b>Discover spill:</b> notify SPCC Coordinator immediately</li><li>If safe to do so, use spill kit / absorbents to contain small releases</li><li>Do not enter contaminated area without proper PPE</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#eef3f9"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fdf6dc;border-color:#8a5a00;color:#111111"><ul><li>Assist with cleanup if directed by SPCC Coordinator</li><li>Provide witness information for Spill Report as requested</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#eef3f9"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#d6eff3;border-color:#1a5c6b;color:#111111"><ul><li>Attend <b>annual oil discharge prevention briefing</b></li><li>Sign Training Record (Appendix 9) to confirm attendance</li><li>Apply lessons from known discharges &amp; malfunctions discussed in briefings</li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><td class="sp-lbl" style="background:#3a1e5f">Operations<br>Team</td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecfa"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#dce9f5;border-color:#2c5f8a;color:#111111"><ul><li>Conduct periodic walkthroughs of entire facility</li><li>Verify master flow &amp; drain valves remain <b>closed</b> when not in use</li><li>Confirm starter controls for oil pumps are <b>off</b> during non-operating status</li><li>Verify loading/unloading connections are capped or blank-flanged when idle</li><li>Confirm adequate lighting is operational for spill discovery</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecfa"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#ece4f5;border-color:#5a3080;color:#111111"><ul><li>Complete <b>monthly AST inspection checklist</b> (Appendix 8)</li><li>Complete <b>monthly portable container checklist</b></li><li>Complete <b>annual AST inspection checklist</b></li><li>Check interstitial leak detection sensors alarm security system</li><li>Check oil water separators and floor drains in generator rooms</li><li>Document all findings; log deficiencies on Corrective Action Log</li><li>Retain completed checklists for <b>at least 36 months</b></li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecfa"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fce8e4;border-color:#8B2500;color:#111111"><ul><li>Discover spills during walkthroughs; notify SPCC Coordinator immediately</li><li>Contain release using spill kit if safe to do so</li><li>Restrict access to affected area</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecfa"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fdf6dc;border-color:#8a5a00;color:#111111"><ul><li>Support cleanup under direction of SPCC Coordinator</li><li>Inspect retained stormwater from secondary containment before releasing</li><li>Document containment drainage events (Appendix 12 &mdash; Drainage Record)</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecfa"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#d6eff3;border-color:#1a5c6b;color:#111111"><ul><li>Maintain Routine Inspection &amp; Corrective Action Log (Appendix 8)</li><li>Record integrity testing results (Appendix 13)</li><li>Retain all inspection and test records with SPCC Plan for <b>min. 3 years</b></li><li>Notify SPCC Coordinator of facility changes that may require plan amendment</li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><td class="sp-lbl" style="background:#1e4a1a">SPCC<br>Coordinator<br>(COM)</td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#e8f5e0"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#dce9f5;border-color:#2c5f8a;color:#111111"><ul><li><b>Accountable person</b> for oil discharge prevention at the facility</li><li>Enforce oil transfer procedure (Appendix 5)</li><li>Ensure spill kits / absorbents are stocked near all oil storage areas</li><li>Maintain copy of SPCC Plan on file at the facility</li><li>Ensure loading/unloading area warning signs and wheel chocks are in place</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#e8f5e0"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#ece4f5;border-color:#5a3080;color:#111111"><ul><li>Oversee monthly &amp; annual AST inspections</li><li>Review inspection logs; assign corrective actions for deficiencies</li><li>Ensure non-conforming items are evaluated by qualified engineer</li><li>Schedule and conduct annual <b>oil discharge prevention briefings</b></li><li>Maintain training records (Appendix 9)</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#e8f5e0"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fce8e4;border-color:#8B2500;color:#111111"><ul><li><b>Receive spill notification</b> from personnel</li><li>Assess: Emergency (fire, HAZMAT, injury) or non-emergency?</li><li>EMERGENCY: Call or direct call to Fire Dept &amp; HAZMAT (911)</li><li>NON-EMERGENCY: Direct containment &amp; absorption at source</li><li>Work: (614) 665-9146 &nbsp;|&nbsp; After Hours: (614) 214-7548</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#e8f5e0"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fdf6dc;border-color:#8a5a00;color:#111111"><ul><li>Direct cleanup or engage Spill Contractor (see Appendix 6) if needed</li><li>Complete <b>Spill Report Form</b> (Appendix 7)</li><li><b>OEPA verbal notice within 30 min</b> if &ge;25 gal, reaches navigable water, or leaves property</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;OEPA: (800) 282-9378 or (614) 224-0946</li><li><b>NRC within 24 hrs</b> if discharged to navigable waters &mdash; (800) 424-8802</li><li>Notify LEPC if release migrates off-site &mdash; Franklin Co.: (614) 794-0213</li><li>Complete <b>written report to OEPA / LEPC within 30 days</b></li><li>Notify EPA Regional Admin <b>within 60 days</b> if &gt;1,000 gal single or &gt;42 gal twice in 12 months</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#e8f5e0"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#d6eff3;border-color:#1a5c6b;color:#111111"><ul><li>File spill documentation with SPCC Plan</li><li>Submit written reports to regulatory agencies within required timeframes</li><li>Evaluate whether spill / facility change requires <b>plan amendment</b></li><li>Implement amendments within <b>6 months</b> of triggering change</li><li>Sign Management Review documentation after 5-year review</li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><td class="sp-lbl" style="background:#5a3000">Spill Cleanup<br>Contractor</td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff3e0"><div class="sp-empty"></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff3e0"><div class="sp-empty"></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff3e0"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fce8e4;border-color:#8B2500;color:#111111"><ul><li><b>Engaged by SPCC Coordinator</b> for large or complex spills</li><li>Respond 24/7 &mdash; see approved contractor list (Appendix 6)</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff3e0"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fdf6dc;border-color:#8a5a00;color:#111111"><ul><li>Contain and recover discharged oil using appropriate methods</li><li>Dispose of recovered oil &amp; contaminated materials per applicable regulations</li><li>Coordinate with SPCC Coordinator on scope and progress</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff3e0"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#d6eff3;border-color:#1a5c6b;color:#111111"><ul><li>Provide cleanup documentation to SPCC Coordinator for SPCC Plan filing</li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><td class="sp-lbl" style="background:#2a1a5c">Management</td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecff"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#dce9f5;border-color:#2c5f8a;color:#111111"><ul><li><b>Approve SPCC Plan</b> at level of authority to commit resources</li><li>Ensure full implementation of SPCC Plan across facility</li><li>Authorized Representative: Matthew Honaker, COM</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecff"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#ece4f5;border-color:#5a3080;color:#111111"><ul><li>Support corrective actions identified during inspections</li><li>Authorize resources for equipment repairs or replacements</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecff"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fce8e4;border-color:#8B2500;color:#111111"><ul><li>Available for serious / major spill events</li><li>Authorize emergency resource commitments if required</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecff"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fdf6dc;border-color:#8a5a00;color:#111111"><ul><li>Authorize major cleanup expenditures as needed</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#f0ecff"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#d6eff3;border-color:#1a5c6b;color:#111111"><ul><li>Conduct <b>5-year management review</b> of entire SPCC Plan</li><li>Amend plan within <b>6 months</b> of review if needed</li><li>Any <b>technical amendments</b> must be certified by a licensed PE</li><li>Document review with signature in Management Review table</li><li>Assess and adopt more effective prevention technology where field-proven</li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><td class="sp-lbl" style="background:#5c1a1a">External<br>Agencies</td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff5f5"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#dce9f5;border-color:#2c5f8a;color:#111111"><ul><li>Regulatory framework: 40 CFR &sect;112 (EPA)</li><li>Ohio SERC: OAC &sect;3750-20 &amp; 25</li><li>Ohio Fire Marshal: OAC &sect;1301-7-7-34 (AST permitting)</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff5f5"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#ece4f5;border-color:#5a3080;color:#111111"><ul><li>May conduct regulatory inspections of facility &amp; SPCC Plan</li><li>SPCC Plan must be available on-site for regulatory review</li><li>Inspection records retained for 3 years per regulatory requirement</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff5f5"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fce8e4;border-color:#8B2500;color:#111111"><ul><li><b>911:</b> Plain Township Fire Dept &amp; HAZMAT response</li><li>Franklin County Sheriff: (614) 855-1234</li><li>LEPC &mdash; Franklin Co. LEPC: (614) 794-0213</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff5f5"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#fdf6dc;border-color:#8a5a00;color:#111111"><ul><li><b>OEPA</b> &mdash; receives verbal notice within 30 min: (800) 282-9378</li><li><b>NRC</b> &mdash; receives notice within 24 hrs: (800) 424-8802</li><li><b>LEPC</b> &mdash; notified if release migrates off-site</li><li><b>EPA Region 5</b> &mdash; receives written report within 60 days if large spill</li><li>OEPA &amp; LEPC receive written report within 30 days (Ohio)</li></ul></div></td><td class="sp-cell" style="background:#fff5f5"><div class="sp-card" style="background:#d6eff3;border-color:#1a5c6b;color:#111111"><ul><li>Receive &amp; process submitted spill reports</li><li>May require plan amendments or additional prevention measures</li><li>Issue inspection findings or violation notices as applicable</li></ul></div></td></tr></tbody>
